==Battleground==
*1 [[Lowkey]] spawns as the boss after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>.
*5 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*5 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*5 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 143.33 seconds<sup>4,300f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*5 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 260 seconds<sup>7,800f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Bore]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Bore]] spawns after 150 seconds<sup>4,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Money is quite scarce and knocking back the Bores will cause your frontlines to move into Lowkey's range, so try not to spawn too many units once you have a Bore locked in place. Once both Bores have been vanquished, you can whittle down Lowkey with [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Dark Emperor Catdam]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] or whatever else you like. A [[Rich Cat]] or a Worker Cat Start Level Up [[Cat Combo|Combo]] can help with money, but neither is required. Since Lowkey can curse any units that could have been used to knock him back, Breakerblast or Sniper is necessary unless said units outrange him.

[[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] or [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Enchantress Cat]] is crucial for stalling the Bores, and 2-4 meatshields are recommended to keep Lowkey from moving. Other useful, albeit unnecessary cats include [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], [[Mecha-Bun (Special Cat)|Ultimate Mecha-Bun]] and [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] attackers such as [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Elemental Duelist Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]].

